# bz/.gitignore
#
# Everything below is machine-local state or a credential. Nothing in this list
# should ever be committed.
#
# NOTE: .env IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED. It holds local-development credentials
# that exist so `docker compose up` works with no setup, and they are labelled as
# such in the file. Do not put anything real in it — a real deployment takes
# these from a secret store, not from a file in the tree.

# PostgreSQL data directories (bind mounts). Recreated by `docker compose up`;
# wiped by `docker compose down -v`.
data/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
